    "description": "The inscription on the back of this magnificent piece reads, \"Fusager Demski 14K,\" accompanied by a distinct maker's mark, a stylized \"M\" with a loop above it, representing the studio name MAGICK. This signature marks an authentic, highly collectible piece of American studio jewelry. This piece was handcrafted during a collaborative partnership between award-winning enamel artist Falcher Fusager and designer Susan Demski. Their joint work dates specifically between 1988 and 2002. They produced jewelry under the studio name MAGICK Fusager Design, Inc., based out of Berkeley, California. Pieces from this era are famous for their masterful, luminescent vitreous cloisonné enamel. The vibrant, multi-layered glass patterns are outlined by fine 24K gold wires fired onto gold bases. The \"14K\" indicates the jewelry is made of solid 14-karat yellow gold.",
